 "id": 588780732634,
 "title": "Gravel Bike by Sebastian",
 "body_html": "<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<div class=\"Qr7Oae\" role=\"listitem\">\n<div class=\"OxAavc NVbRL\" jsname=\"ibnC6b\" jscontroller=\"rDGJeb\" jsaction=\"sPvj8e:e4JwSe,Dlbleb;O22p3e:e4JwSe,F0zejc;\" data-required=\"true\" data-item-id=\"680938726\">\n<div class=\"pYfr3c\">\n<div class=\"prOLdf\">\n<div class=\"g53bl\">\n<h4 class=\"cTDvob D1wxyf RjsPE\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" aria-describedby=\"i.desc.680938726 c476\"><strong><span class=\"M7eMe\">What made you decide to build a bamboo bike?</span></strong></h4>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Ih4Dzb\">\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\">I wanted a gravel bike that was comfortable, light, and had better vibration control. I heard from an Global Cycling Network video that bamboo bikes dampened vibrations better, so I built a bamboo bike. (also they look cool)</div>\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Qr7Oae\" role=\"listitem\">\n<div class=\"OxAavc NVbRL\" jsname=\"ibnC6b\" jscontroller=\"rDGJeb\" jsaction=\"sPvj8e:e4JwSe,Dlbleb;O22p3e:e4JwSe,F0zejc;\" data-item-id=\"845063547\">\n<div class=\"pYfr3c\">\n<div class=\"prOLdf\">\n<h4 class=\"g53bl\"><strong><span class=\"M7eMe\">Did you enjoy building the bicycle from scratch and would you recommend the experience?</span></strong></h4>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Ih4Dzb\">\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\">It was a lot of fun to do and I'm now able to say they I built up a bike all by myself. My frame has some imperfections, but I think it adds more charm to the bike. I would recommend this experience to anybody who likes to build their own stuff, and is cool when things might not go exactly as planned.</div>\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Qr7Oae\" role=\"listitem\">\n<div class=\"OxAavc NVbRL\" jsname=\"ibnC6b\" jscontroller=\"rDGJeb\" jsaction=\"sPvj8e:e4JwSe,Dlbleb;O22p3e:e4JwSe,F0zejc;\" data-required=\"true\" data-item-id=\"805044919\">\n<div class=\"pYfr3c\">\n<div class=\"prOLdf\">\n<div class=\"g53bl\">\n<h4 class=\"cTDvob D1wxyf RjsPE\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" aria-describedby=\"i.desc.805044919 c481\"><strong><span class=\"M7eMe\">What did you find most difficult about your bike build?</span></strong></h4>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Ih4Dzb\">\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\">The most difficult part of it had to be the component fitting. The rear triangle of my frame ended up being a little wonky, so the parts I purchased wouldn't fit on it properly. to avoid running into this issue, I would suggest waiting to buy your components until after you finish the frame.</div>\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\"></div>\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Qr7Oae\" role=\"listitem\">\n<div class=\"OxAavc NVbRL\" jsname=\"ibnC6b\" jscontroller=\"rDGJeb\" jsaction=\"sPvj8e:e4JwSe,Dlbleb;O22p3e:e4JwSe,F0zejc;\" data-item-id=\"1370153519\">\n<div class=\"pYfr3c\">\n<div class=\"prOLdf\">\n<div class=\"g53bl\">\n<h4 class=\"cTDvob D1wxyf RjsPE\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" aria-describedby=\"i.desc.1370153519\"><strong><span class=\"M7eMe\">What was the easiest part of the build?</span></strong></h4>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Ih4Dzb\">\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\">The easiest part of the build would be shaping the ends of the bamboo. It took a lot of time as I only had 80 grit sandpaper, but it was easy.</div>\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\"></div>\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Qr7Oae\" role=\"listitem\">\n<div class=\"OxAavc NVbRL\" jsname=\"ibnC6b\" jscontroller=\"rDGJeb\" jsaction=\"sPvj8e:e4JwSe,Dlbleb;O22p3e:e4JwSe,F0zejc;\" data-required=\"true\" data-item-id=\"862135650\">\n<div class=\"pYfr3c\">\n<div class=\"prOLdf\">\n<div class=\"g53bl\">\n<h4 class=\"cTDvob D1wxyf RjsPE\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" aria-describedby=\"i.desc.862135650 c486\"><strong><span class=\"M7eMe\">How would you describe the ride of your finished bike?</span></strong></h4>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Ih4Dzb\">\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\">Smooth and quick.</div>\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Qr7Oae\" role=\"listitem\">\n<div class=\"OxAavc NVbRL\" jsname=\"ibnC6b\" jscontroller=\"rDGJeb\" jsaction=\"sPvj8e:e4JwSe,Dlbleb;O22p3e:e4JwSe,F0zejc;\" data-required=\"true\" data-item-id=\"1476906189\">\n<div class=\"pYfr3c\">\n<div class=\"prOLdf\">\n<div class=\"g53bl\">\n<h4 class=\"cTDvob D1wxyf RjsPE\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" aria-describedby=\"i.desc.1476906189 c489\"><span class=\"M7eMe\">What would you improve about the build experience or your finished bike?</span></h4>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"Ih4Dzb\">\n<div class=\"q4tvle JqSWld yqQS1\">I would buy my own components to ensure they work properly with my frame, and I would put weights on top of the jig to make sure it doesn't move while the glue is drying.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
 "blog_id": 73142304951,
